base Image which is present in docker hub
docker run python or docker run node21 --alphine
uper wali file docker me hoti hai us ko apen Docker file me likhte hai
aise
- From python or FROM node:${NODE_VERSION}-alpine as base (alphine docker image ki side reduce karne ke liye)
 - From python:3.8-alphine
phir entry point project ka
- ADD app.py /tree/app.py-> /app is destination folder

command entry file ko run karne ke liye
- CMD ["python","/tree/app.py"]



build docker command
- docker build -t python-hello-world(image name) .(which directory . show ager single . hai to current .. hai to bahar)
  - docker build -t python-hello-world:V2(build with tag name)
   - docker run python-hello-world:V2 (run with tag name)

change working dir
 - WORKDIR /tree

- docker dongling images remove
  - docker rmi ${docker images dangling=true} -f
  - docker rmi imageId
  - docker ps
  - docker stop imageId
  - docker images ls dangling=true
 - remove all dangling image
  - docker image prune 

- Remove docker container
  - docker rm containerId
  - docker rm  ${docker ps -aq} (docker ps -aq common container remove with different containerId)

-check docker is running
	- docker ps



